    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1029">

                <pb facs="1198" n="1002" xml:id="pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1029<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador
                        in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1029-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-18">July 18, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 68. For Ambassador Winant, London,
                    repeated to State Department, Washington from Secretary of State, Berlin.</p>
                <p>U. S. and U. K. military authorities in Germany agree that French Berlin area of
                    occupation will be formed from existing U. K. and U. S. areas.</p>
                <p>As soon as U. K. representative EAC<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1029-f2"/> have [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">has</hi>] received similar instructions, you are
                    authorized accept Soviet July 12th [<hi rendition="#italic">11th</hi>]
                        proposal<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1029-f3"/> for final sentence report
                    accompanying agreement on French Zone in Germany and conclude agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
